    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe create pipeline is `POST /api/owners`, wired as OfficeFloor functions in `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`. I added one step between `save` and `respond` so the audit line is only emitted after a successful persist (owner id assigned) but as part of the successful create path.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- Reads the persisted `@Val Owner`.\n- Logs via the dedicated `AUDIT` logger (`LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`) an info line carrying the owner `id`, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 in `owners.POST.yml`, inserted an `audit` step (`save \u2192 audit \u2192 respond`), under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbours.\n\n## Why here\n- After `SaveOwner`, the JPA-assigned id is populated, and `customerCode` (set by `AssignCustomerCode`) and `registrationDate` (set by `BuildOwner`) are on the entity \u2014 all three the test reads back from `GET /api/owners/{id}` and asserts appear in one AUDIT line.\n- Before `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, so the line is written only on the successful path.\n- `LocalDate.toString()` produces the ISO form (e.g. `2026-08-10`), matching the JSON `registrationDate` text the test compares against.\n\n## Verification\n`AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` passes, and the observed log line was:\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-10\n```\nFull `./mvnw test`: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
